    "narrative": "The Austin Waves look toward a high-upside evening led by **Luis Garc\u00eda Jr.** (73.66) and **Kyle Tucker** (71.28). **Luis Garc\u00eda Jr.** benefits from a favorable matchup against Pecko, whose 5.95 xERA provides a massive boost to his base projection, further amplified by a strong platoon advantage and a prime spot in the three-hole. Similarly, **Kyle Tucker** remains an essential start against Elder, leveraging his elite base profile to overcome the mid-tier xERA of his opponent. While **Vladimir Guerrero Jr.** (69.26) faces a tougher hurdle with his platoon split, his power profile against Lugo keeps him squarely in the strong-start category for today\u2019s utility slot.\n\nThe most difficult decision on the roster involves the benching of **Miguel Vargas**, who narrowly missed the cut with a score of 39.60. While his 0.389 xwOBA is encouraging, the daunting task of facing deGrom\u2014combined with a neutral platoon profile and an elite opposing hold\u2014drove his score just below our 40.0 efficiency floor. Elsewhere, we remain cautious regarding our speed-dependent outfielders; **Jackson Merrill** (48.97) and **Luis Robert Jr.** (50.56) both carry significant risk today. Facing elite catchers and high-skill arms like Skenes, their ability to generate value in our scarcest category, Stolen Bases, is neutralized by the opposition's ability to control the running game.\n\nWe are monitoring the status of the lineup closely, as the proximity of **Gunnar Henderson** (53.04) and **Coby Mayo** (53.15) to the 50-point threshold against Liberatore leaves little room for error. While both possess the talent to anchor the team, the platoon disadvantage against a left-handed starter necessitates that we keep a close eye on any late defensive changes. With **Jordan Westburg**, **Andy Pages**, and **Jacob Wilson** sidelined on the IL, our depth is thin, placing the burden of production squarely on the shoulders of our active starters to maintain our Roto standings.",
